`stdio.h` – Contains standard input and output functions.
`stdlib.h` – Provides utility functions such as `exit()`.
`unistd.h` – Provides system calls like `fork()`, `getpid()` and `getppid()`.
`sys/wait.h` – Contains functions used for process synchronization, such as `wait()`.
`fork()` – Creates a new process called the child process.
`pid_t` – Data type used to store process IDs.
`getpid()` – Returns the process ID of the current process.
`getppid()` – Returns the process ID of the parent process.
`wait()` – Suspends the parent process until a child process finishes.
`exit(0)` – Ends the process with successful execution status.
`printf()` – Displays output on the terminal.
`if (pid == 0)` – Identifies whether the executing process is the child process.
`else` – Executes the statements associated with the parent process.
